      objectReference: {fileID: 1189327141}
    - target: {fileID: 7218531343177372468, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: 'buttons.Array.data[2]'
      value: 
      objectReference: {fileID: 1189327140}
    - target: {fileID: 7218531343177372468, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: textDataList.Array.size
      value: 3
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7218531343177372468, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: textDataList.Array.data[0].subText
      value: "A Vernier Caliper is a mechanical measuring instrument used for precise
        measurements of length, depth, internal and external diameters of an object.
        It combines a main scale and a sliding vernier scale, which allows users
        to read measurements with a high degree of accuracy \u2014 often up to 0.02
        mm.\n\nInvented by Pierre Vernier in 1631, the vernier caliper works on the
        principle of alignment between the vernier and main scale markings to determine
        precise fractional measurements that are smaller than the smallest divisions
        on the main scale.\n\n"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7218531343177372468, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: textDataList.Array.data[1].subText
      value: "A **screw gauge**, also known as a **micrometer screw gauge**, is a
        precision instrument used to measure very small lengths, thicknesses, or
        diameters of objects with high accuracy, usually up to 0.01 mm. It operates
        on the principle of a screw, where the rotation of a calibrated screw translates
        into linear movement, allowing fine measurements. It\u2019s commonly used
        in mechanical, engineering, and physics laboratories for detailed dimensional
        analysis."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7218531343177372468, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: textDataList.Array.data[2].subText
      value: A **spherometer** is a precision instrument used to measure the curvature
        (radius of curvature) of spherical surfaces, such as lenses and mirrors.
        It typically consists of a central screw and three outer legs that form a
        triangle. The central screw moves up and down and measures the height difference
        between the curved surface and a reference plane. This height is used in
        a formula to calculate the radius of curvature of the sphere.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7218531343177372468, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: textDataList.Array.data[0].mainText
      value: Vernier Callipers
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7218531343177372468, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: textDataList.Array.data[1].mainText
      value: Screw Guage
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7218531343177372468, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: textDataList.Array.data[2].mainText
      value: Spherometer
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 8208273231042760615, guid: 5deb76e381698fe4ea6a79222c0ec44d, type: 3}
      propertyPath: subText
